{
  "about": "The Edit menu acts on the focused text field, as a Mac's first responder takes it (docs/adr/0021-menu-bar.mdx, decision 3): sample/EditMenuProbe.tsx (launched as Allo) declares with Bloom's Menubar a Mac's Edit menu, each standard item a `MenubarItem action` (Undo, Redo, Cut, Copy, Paste, Paste and Match Style, Delete, Select All), its Copy also the application's own (it copies the page's selected item), and Find… the application's command; a second application, EditMenuPeer, is the same page. Each step checks the window's menus exactly as the shell is told them (every Edit item enabled or disabled), the field's text and selection as React receives them, exactly the React events of both applications, what each client was delivered, focus and the clipboard: with no field focused the items are the application's (its own Copy runs, once); a field focused is the first responder and each item is enabled exactly as the field validates it (Copy with a selection, Paste with text on the clipboard, Undo with an edit, Cut and Copy never in a secure field) and acts on it, from the shell's bar with the pointer or by the `menu` step; after a menu of the bar the keyboard is the window's again; the field keeps its own chords (Ctrl+A, Ctrl+X) and Bloom takes Paste and Match Style's; and the clipboard goes from one application's field to the other's and back through Edit > Copy and Paste. Without the adapter's `editing` every item but the application's own stays as the application declared it and the editing steps fail; with the top bar taking the keyboard on a press, the keys after a bar's menu and its Copy are lost.",
  "locale": "es_ES.UTF-8",
  "module": "EditMenuProbe",
  "window": [
    380,
    420
  ],
  "shell": "OxyOSShell",
  "app": {
    "id": "so.oxy.allo",
    "title": "Allo"
  },
  "companion": {
    "module": "EditMenuPeer",
